<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:48Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Russia bans two French lawmakers and two journalists from entry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3645f23b949e5bc35b9ff59d723b04707705de8416eb15738a1da3b827e00a3a</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:58:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-bans-two-french-lawmakers-and-two-journalists-from-entry--647f8165ba44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-bans-two-french-lawmakers-and-two-journalists-from-entry" /><summary type="html">Moscow on Wednesday said it was banning two French journalists and two French lawmakers from entering Russia in response to Paris's expulsion of pro-Russian TV commentator Xenia Fedorova earlier this year.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: General strike over housing costs before national election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cb3193d49677c1258d7fd8ac5ef775068b856733bbcf7d868037cb8948a6b59</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:54:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-general-strike-over-housing-costs-before-national-election--d795ce513ad5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-general-strike-over-housing-costs-before-national-election" /><summary type="html">Millions of Spanish workers shut down businesses and public transportation in a protest on Wednesday over housing costs that the government hopes to leverage before a national election later this month. The walkout — under the slogan “Salaries. Housing. Prices.” — was the first general strike in Spain in 14 years.</summary></entry><entry><title>Exclusive: EU's Kallas says US 'can't negotiate on our behalf' on lifting Russia sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cd1af68f3cdb0f5d05a0445cb946836d6eda17c84a91c22b66109f848ec4089</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:15:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261111-exclusive-eu-s-kallas-says-us-can-t-negotiate-on-our-behalf-on-lifting-russia-sanctions--7f31e05dcc4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261111-exclusive-eu-s-kallas-says-us-can-t-negotiate-on-our-behalf-on-lifting-russia-sanctions" /><summary type="html">In an exclusive interview with FRANCE 24, the EU's top diplomat Kaja Kallas discusses the war in Ukraine, the situation in the Middle East and a possible change in US President Donald Trump's foreign policy following the US midterm elections. The former Estonian prime minister, who is now the European Union's High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy, also reaffirms the EU's position as a major player on the global geopolitical stage.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Aneto, one of southern Europe's largest glaciers, is melting away</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa30a57158ee59afa925cf839d2bc4afa8ba8022456bae626ac82fba7bd3adf0</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:32:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261111-aneto-one-of-southern-europe-s-largest-glaciers-is-melting-away--7bca17aca8fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261111-aneto-one-of-southern-europe-s-largest-glaciers-is-melting-away" /><summary type="html">Within a decade, one of the largest glaciers in southern Europe will have disappeared. Aneto, the highest peak of the Spanish Pyrenees, is melting at a spectacular rate. Its demise is another sign of global warming and has much to teach glaciologists. FRANCE 24's Maude Petit-Jové, Mathilde Lopinski and Sarah Morris report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Patrick Bury: 'It’s going to cost a lot of money to repair the systems.'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcee0fe3f07068638c0254e493d574514ad674bf6256673a7fcfbb3d11415c6e</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:32:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-how-prepared-is-the-continent-to-face-a-futur-conflict--d7020f165247.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-how-prepared-is-the-continent-to-face-a-futur-conflict" /><summary type="html">Patrick Bury, Senior associate professor in warfare and counterterrorism at University of Bath, is our guest.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK comedian David Walliams accused of grooming and sexual harassment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2960c932574a6ab6fa0c25fa8ad3d07e122f495347b4ce0c31083eebec55b3d9</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:23:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:56:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261111-uk-comedian-david-walliams-accused-of-grooming-and-sexual-harassment--5fccf1ffbe7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261111-uk-comedian-david-walliams-accused-of-grooming-and-sexual-harassment" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, November 11: Spanish and French papers discuss protests in the two countries. An investigation by The Guardian and ITV accuses comedian David Walliams of "preying on young women for sex". Finally, a Doberman sensed something was wrong with a baby. It may have saved his life.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Wave of hoax bomb threats sent to schools in UK, Ireland and Italy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c421b94824203a5ee75a701e69d75c0808a06262210c1f4f677ff3f08a6020df</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:57:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-hundreds-of-schools-in-italy-evacuated-after-receiving-bomb-threats--967169548911.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-hundreds-of-schools-in-italy-evacuated-after-receiving-bomb-threats" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of schools in the UK, Italy and the Republic of Ireland received a "generic" threatening email on Wednesday now being treated as a hoax by authorities. Italy earlier evacuated roughly 300 schools over the perceived threat.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia, Ukraine start second day of US-led talks: Kyiv lead negotiator</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1246e7ad910c733a83f704901d5748ec4611e89bec9e9b46d4c1facc3fdb744c</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:42:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-ukraine-start-second-day-of-us-led-talks-kyiv-lead-negotiator--ce553d61579f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-ukraine-start-second-day-of-us-led-talks-kyiv-lead-negotiator" /><summary type="html">Russia and Ukraine have resumed US-mediated talks in Abu Dhabi for a second day, Kyiv's chief negotiator Rustem Umerov said on Wednesday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's first general strike in 14 years, 3 weeks before national polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5617c5cb45c0f03ee54227cda0f351a34a6a6b721f09e8fda497b30af1e547a3</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:30:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-s-first-general-strike-in-14-years-3-weeks-before-national-polls--7baf50b0712f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-s-first-general-strike-in-14-years-3-weeks-before-national-polls" /><summary type="html">Sarah Morris is live from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Portugal shuts schools, tech conference as it braces for storm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c960b0a11201c96445c9bceaf87b85d7d5011b7a0261c26d301f33361dd8f77e</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/portugal-shuts-schools-tech-conference-as-it-braces-for-storm--85bdf5a4749a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/portugal-shuts-schools-tech-conference-as-it-braces-for-storm" /><summary type="html">Portugal said it would shut schools, non-essential services and a top world tech conference on Wednesday, as it braces for gale-force winds of Storm Charles.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK authorities arrest US soldier suspected of spying for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:195cca878194c28162841644d4c98ab589ec1e116720d70b6a2b2316772fa0aa</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T09:41:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/uk-authorities-arrests-us-soldier-suspected-of-spying-for-russia--305fec5257b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/uk-authorities-arrests-us-soldier-suspected-of-spying-for-russia" /><summary type="html">A member of the US army suspected of spying for Russia was arrested in Britain on Tuesday, London police said, following an investigation with support from the American military and law enforcement.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain’s general strike puts housing crisis at centre of upcoming elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dff9aee7a47dba181819f55e85e0742d5ab4e9a07eb3ddcf9153293eeff89dcf</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:24:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T08:29:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-spain-general-strike-puts-housing-crisis-centre-upcoming-elections--d80411702cc0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-spain-general-strike-puts-housing-crisis-centre-upcoming-elections" /><summary type="html">Millions of Spanish workers are striking Wednesday – the first general strike in 14 years – to demand action on a major housing crisis and the rising cost of living. The expected disruptions to public transport and the widespread closure of businesses come less than three weeks before a snap election that could bring the far right to power.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Live: US envoys to meet Putin in Moscow, Zelensky in Dublin after Abu Dhabi talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fcb196a08ad31c11f6893e8c5e39d455beb68c8ddaa53e410fbb08421bd94f2</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T03:22:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-live-ukraine-russia-hold-second-day-of-us-mediated-talks-in-abu-dhabi--18813df16781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-live-ukraine-russia-hold-second-day-of-us-mediated-talks-in-abu-dhabi" /><summary type="html">US envoys Jared Kushner and Steve Witkoff will fly to Moscow Thursday to meet Russian President Vladimir Putin and later hold talks with Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky in Dublin, Kushner told reporters in Abu Dhabi on Wednesday after a second day of UAE-hosted talks. Moscow's top envoy said the two sides had agreed to a major prisoner swap. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Europe not going anywhere': G7 summit a 'signal to Russians' that Europe is standing behind Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e43efc7b2980a1cc8e91b62eca34d2e8e508e911500f0892a3122833d9506716</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T21:57:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-not-going-anywhere-g7-summit-a-signal-to-russians-that-europe-is-standing-behind-ukraine--7a75adc507db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-not-going-anywhere-g7-summit-a-signal-to-russians-that-europe-is-standing-behind-ukraine" /><summary type="html">As the US Midterms reshape Ukraine diplomacy, Annette Young is pleased to welcome James Townsend, Atlantic Council's Senior Advisor at the Scowcroft Center's for Transatlantic Security Initiative. "Europe is not going anywhere." With this unequivocal assessment, Townsend, taking place alongside trilateral negotiations in Abu Dhabi. While the latter may command international attention, Townsend argues that the Paris meeting carries a message of its own: European support for Ukraine is intended to remain durable, and Moscow should not mistake diplomatic negotiations for an erosion of Western resolve. The G7 meeting therefore emerges as more than a forum for diplomatic declarations. It represents a test of Western cohesion, the credibility of future military and financial assistance, and Washington's willingness to endorse a common position on Ukraine. As Townsend emphasizes, the final communiqué will also be "a test as far as what Marco Rubio is going to agree to put his name to."</summary></entry><entry><title>Asymmetric cyberwarfare: 'States increasingly use cyberattacks in support of their other objectives'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8df99d4cbee983353ffaca7bdd7483bb21473d1b4eda74b6ce73a0945ee5ba2e</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T21:25:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asymmetric-cyberwarfare-states-increasingly-use-cyberattacks-in-support-of-their-other-objectives--937e2d10d52d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asymmetric-cyberwarfare-states-increasingly-use-cyberattacks-in-support-of-their-other-objectives" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Rafe Pilling, Director of Threat Intelligence in the Sophos Counter Threat Unit (CTU). How can a minor cyber intrusion disrupt food supplies, expose the weaknesses of industrial infrastructure and become an instrument of geopolitical confrontation? The cyberattacks targeting supermarket refrigeration systems in France offer a revealing illustration of how digital vulnerabilities can translate into tangible economic disruption and potentially broader threats to society. As Pilling explains, “With a small amount of effort from the adversary side, they can create a large impact, in this case destroying food and producing empty shelves or empty refrigeration units in stores.” This asymmetry lies at the heart of contemporary cyber conflict, in which modest technical interventions can produce disproportionate economic and operational consequences</summary></entry><entry><title>US soldier arrested in Britain on suspicion of assisting Russian intelligence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c371ea5beba428f598c2c332d12d3d9e352d3c08c1d3d9779d7e054efc5f79b9</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T20:23:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-us-soldier-arrested-in-britain-on-suspicion-of-assisting-russian-intelligence--9083470d25a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-us-soldier-arrested-in-britain-on-suspicion-of-assisting-russian-intelligence" /><summary type="html">UK police arrested a senior member of the US Army on Tuesday on suspicion of assisting Russian intelligence, adding that the arrest was not related to other counter-terror investigations. The 41-year-old man was detained near the city of Gloucester, west England, and remains in custody.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>What the hack? Europeans face growing psyops and cyberattacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c3e4ad0a8b936939df379b2fef2a5922a3dbb8a41e65f7baa5e3a9cd199bbe2</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T20:19:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261110-what-the-hack-europeans-face-growing-psyops-and-cyberattacks--2cfcf95d4999.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261110-what-the-hack-europeans-face-growing-psyops-and-cyberattacks" /><summary type="html">So this time, it's Iran, not Russia? France – reportedly acting on US intelligence – is summoning Tehran's ambassador over last month's hacking of hundreds of supermarket refrigerators that overheated, 15 of which even caught fire. Why now, at a time when Iran is trying to break its international isolation?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Kristallnacht's 88th anniversary: Merz says Germany faces historic test over anti-Semitism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7661c3d0da19459d2a3ade7d90f999a77c0d4a4af57754f02f08c53a8af8f3c9</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T16:47:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-kristallnacht-88th-anniversary-merz-says-germany-faces-historic-test-over-antisemitism--a526c9837a2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-kristallnacht-88th-anniversary-merz-says-germany-faces-historic-test-over-antisemitism" /><summary type="html">It has been 88 years since "Kristallnacht", the "Night of Broken Glass" in Europe, a violent pogrom against the Jewish population across Nazi Germany and Austria that marked a critical escalation toward the Holocaust. German Chanceller Friedrich Merz said that his country currently faces a historic test over anti-Semitism.</summary></entry><entry><title>French students vow to keep up protest pressure for better learning conditions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d4bcfef41a24fe01d6a867c32fb4b1fab42b7c437d753555ac8e0a2df32df89</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T16:40:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-french-students-vow-to-keep-up-protest-pressure-for-better-learning-conditions--a9381299c60b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-french-students-vow-to-keep-up-protest-pressure-for-better-learning-conditions" /><summary type="html">France has been buffeted for months by street protests. They began in September ​with students ‌demanding the renovation of school buildings, more teachers and ⁠university reforms but then turned into broader cost-of-living protests, drawing in trade unions and political activists, and sometimes ‌turning violent.</summary></entry><entry><title>US-mediated talks on ending Russia-Ukraine war begin in Abu Dhabi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a7622e481d9798c9c48ed4b83cc80738a4eac697a4abb3c02f3daebca51ae43</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:29:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-us-mediated-talks-on-ending-russia-ukraine-war-begin-in-abu-dhabi--79da08e24fd7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-us-mediated-talks-on-ending-russia-ukraine-war-begin-in-abu-dhabi" /><summary type="html">Three-way talks between Russia, Ukraine and the US opened Tuesday, November 10, in the United Arab Emirates, as Washington made another push to end the war. The two-day session in Abu Dhabi is the first such meeting since February. It will focus on establishing future security guarantees for the warring countries.</summary></entry><entry><title>French students block dozens of schools, vow more protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff5cc7a4c34d893048adf6cab296d55c830998370d70ee8f301b7dce73d5fe29</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:29:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-french-students-block-dozens-of-schools-vow-more-protests--1de30cb67916.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-french-students-block-dozens-of-schools-vow-more-protests" /><summary type="html">French students blocked the entrances to dozens of high schools on Tuesday, November 10, as they kept up protests for better learning conditions. These protests across France have spiraled into larger cost-of-living demonstrations in recent weeks, some marked by violence and police brutality. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>France vows tough response to freezer cyberattack blamed on Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:423fde15c830c10a2ade2250e17295c1f8442d4563b2f7b8934501db146292bd</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:51:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-france-vows-tough-response-to-freezer-cyberattack-blamed-on-iran--fb059c4de0f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-france-vows-tough-response-to-freezer-cyberattack-blamed-on-iran" /><summary type="html">France's Foreign Minister Jean-Noel Barrot said Tuesday, November 10, that Paris ruled out "nothing" to respond to a major cyberattack on hundreds of supermarket fridges in October that it has blamed on Iran. The goal, Jean-Noel Barrot told France Info, is "to deter anyone who might be tempted, in Iran or elsewhere, to do it again".</summary></entry><entry><title>Seniors rock the stage: Greek theater seeks to show that 'art has no age'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0fcd47808a781b447011006268fd2f8aa0eacf93e55c52776999865a4a5c475b</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:50:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-seniors-rock-the-stage-greek-theater-seeks-to-show-that-art-has-no-age--d63b9739c4e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-seniors-rock-the-stage-greek-theater-seeks-to-show-that-art-has-no-age" /><summary type="html">A recent Greek National Opera production afforded a group of seniors the chance to channel their young-at-heart energy into onstage performances, proving that no one's too old to learn something new. It challenged the premise that retirement means surrendering to a sedentary lifestyle and extinguishing one’s creative spirit.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia and Ukraine hold US-backed talks after Trump says broad deal is possible</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52da7a0f6a7dba820cee628c17a7c752aef76654e148d694d528e98a5f9d4fd7</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:40:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-russia-and-ukraine-hold-us-backed-talks-after-trump-says-broad-deal-is-possible--727bc2af7a06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-russia-and-ukraine-hold-us-backed-talks-after-trump-says-broad-deal-is-possible" /><summary type="html">Russian and Ukrainian officials met on Tuesday, November 10, for their first US-brokered talks since February, after US President Donald Trump suggested last week that a broad deal was possible on ending the war in Ukraine and guaranteeing security in Europe. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kyiv Emmanuelle Chaze and FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Rochelle Ferguson have more.</summary></entry><entry><title>First day of Ukraine-Russia talks 'constructive and quite substantive', Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa8e95a231ecfbaa05ea83f73304a71e556ddb7a90bc5bff894a7e56276029f6</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T06:09:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-live-ukraine-russia-and-us-to-resume-peace-talks-in-abu-dhabi--54a00d669ba5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-live-ukraine-russia-and-us-to-resume-peace-talks-in-abu-dhabi" /><summary type="html">Negotiators from Ukraine, Russia and the United States met for their first trilateral talks in more than nine months in Abu Dhabi on Tuesday, as Washington seeks to broker an end to the war and Kyiv faces pressure over territorial concessions. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio hailed the talks as "very productive" and said the discussions should be expanded to include Europeans at the table. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky calls Ukraine-Russia talks 'constructive', Rubio wants Europe 'at the table'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f93c0f774b532e741c6141e6b5e9cfe1e2a130175ed92ab53eb771d5648669d</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T03:01:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-zelensky-calls-ukraine-russia-talks-constructive-rubio-wants-europe-at-the-table--4f2497198512.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-zelensky-calls-ukraine-russia-talks-constructive-rubio-wants-europe-at-the-table" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio on Tuesday hailed US-mediated talks between Russia and Ukraine in Abu Dhabi as "very productive" and said the discussions should be expanded to include Europeans at the table. Ukraine's Volodymyr Zelensky described the talks as "constructive and quite substantive", adding that negotiators were working on a possible major exchange of prisoners.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK writer M. John Harrison wins Booker Prize for AI-tinged apocalyptic novel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2670fcd7f9c109c38f3da30b339882f4579da5ed812792881447a15830e4b984</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T22:09:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-uk-writer-m-john-harrison-wins-booker-prize-for-ai-tinged-apocalyptic-novel--baced25ef4ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-uk-writer-m-john-harrison-wins-booker-prize-for-ai-tinged-apocalyptic-novel" /><summary type="html">UK author M. John Harrison won the Booker Prize on Monday for his enigmatic novel "The End of Everything", which echoes concerns about artificial intelligence in a darkly satirical depiction of post-apocalyptic Britain.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>What to expect as Russia, Ukraine and the US hold trilateral talks in Abu Dhabi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:882f0d33a601e69bb1511342fdf25493f985cc8785e4bd8c8c31cc86ac8b1601</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T21:46:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-what-to-expect-as-russia-ukraine-and-us-hold-trilateral-talks-in-abu-dhabi--07b759c50f93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-what-to-expect-as-russia-ukraine-and-us-hold-trilateral-talks-in-abu-dhabi" /><summary type="html">Negotiators from Ukraine, Russia and the United States are set to meet in the capital of the United Arab Emirates (UAE) on Tuesday for a new round of talks aimed at ending nearly five years of full-scale war triggered by Moscow's invasion of its neighbour. Security guarantees for the warring sides are set to top the agenda, with US officials insisting that a broader security architecture for Europe must be part of any peace deal.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Paris prosecutor opens probe into IRGC cyber unit Shahid Kaveh over fridge cyberattacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5e1da75d7440c67a2070df111f9b863eea27c6ac39e66824fc43c3dd186bf8b</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:06:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/paris-prosecutor-opens-probe-into-irgc-cyber-unit-shahid-kaveh-over-fridge-cyberattacks--f78cb38b635a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/paris-prosecutor-opens-probe-into-irgc-cyber-unit-shahid-kaveh-over-fridge-cyberattacks" /><summary type="html">The Paris prosecutor said she had opened an investigation into Shahid Kaveh, a shadowy cyber unit of the IRGC, the Islamic republic's ideological army, over the 'unprecedented' cyberattacks targeting French supermarkets' fridges in October. Little is known about the Shahid Kaveh unit, although analysts have long observed that the IRGC, which has a vast network of operations, had actively branched out into cyber warfare in recent years. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Sexual predator' Russell Brand jailed for 10 years for rape, assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d6ebbc8049af01236b565b2734ea98fbf644b0c1a465c83960477e59e42462c</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:03:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault--03265434b707.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault" /><summary type="html">British comedian and TV star Russell Brand was Monday jailed for more than 10 years for a string of sex offences including rape, as the judge told him he had been a "sexual predator" whose fame had protected him. Brand, 51, showed no emotion as judge Joel Bennathan said he had acted with "staggering arrogance" and shown "contempt" for his victims, who had suffered significant and lasting harm. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.</summary></entry></feed>
